uestions-facing-investigators/articleshow/134614044.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 14:53:04 +0530</pubDate><dc:creator>AADRITA HALDER</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" length="115482" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134614149,imgsize-115482.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Finance ministry projects 7.3% Q2 growth as economy maintains momentum]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/finance-ministry-projects-7-3-q2-growth-as-economy-maintains-momentum/articleshow/134621094.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/finance-ministry-projects-7-3-q2-growth-as-economy-maintains-momentum/articleshow/134621094.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 19:42:17 +0530</pubDate><dc:creator>YASHASVI VASISTHA</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" length="91968" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134621713,imgsize-91968.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India, Pakistan, Australia in same group for 2027 ODI World Cup]]></title><description><![CDATA[India and Pakistan, along with Australia, will be part of Group A in the upcoming 2027 ICC Men's ODI World Cup. The tournament is set to take place in South Africa, Zimbabwe, and Namibia, starting on October 2 and concluding on November 21. A total of 14 teams will participate, divided into two groups of six after a preliminary stage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/cricket/news/india-pakistan-australia-in-same-group-for-2027-odi-world-cup/articleshow/134623247.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/cricket/news/india-pakistan-australia-in-same-group-for-2027-odi-world-cup/articleshow/134623247.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 21:34:23 +0530</pubDate><dc:creator>AMIT KUMAR</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" length="32273" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134623259,imgsize-32273.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Unimaginable grief: 8 Pune students on school picnic drown at Diveagar beach]]></title><description><![CDATA[A picnic at Diveagar beach turned tragic when eight students from Pune drowned after being swept away. They misjudged the sea's depth and current strength, leading to their distress. Local authorities and rescue teams responded promptly to recover all eight bodies. Maharashtra ministers expressed their condolences and sought details regarding the incident. Legal and administrative procedures are currently being conducted at the site of the tragedy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/pune/motionless-bodies-desperate-hands-heartbreaking-scenes-at-diveagar-beach-as-locals-fight-to-save-pune-students-what-we-know/articleshow/134621926.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/pune/motionless-bodies-desperate-hands-heartbreaking-scenes-at-diveagar-beach-as-locals-fight-to-save-pune-students-what-we-know/articleshow/134621926.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 20:01:31 +0530</pubDate><dc:creator>TOI CITY DESK</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" length="62069" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134621989,imgsize-62069.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Smiling &amp; laughing': India's envoy to UAE meets flydubai hero pilot Smit Machchhar]]></title><description><![CDATA[Indian ambassador Deepak Mittal visited Captain Smit Machchhar at the hospital following the stabbing incident. Captain Machchhar was attacked by his co-pilot while flying from Dubai to Tel Aviv. After the initial treatment in Saudi Arabia, he was airlifted to Abu Dhabi for further medical care. Passengers and two other pilots helped to restrain the attacker and safely landed the flight.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/in-good-health-recovering-well-indian-ambassador-meets-injured-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar/articleshow/134621513.cms]]></link><gui